# Copy to `config/topics.private.yaml` and point at it with
# `PIPELINE_TOPICS_FILE` in `.env`, or with `global_batch.topics_file` in
# `config/pipeline.yaml`. The real file is gitignored (`*.private.yaml`),
# because a channel's topic list is its editorial line and does not belong in
# a public repository.
#
# Same shape as the `topics:` block in `config/pipeline.yaml` and as a
# `--topics-file`. `keywords` seed the stock search when the script-derived
# phrases are unavailable; they are not the primary source.
- title: "Why your wifi keeps dropping"
  description: "Router placement, channel congestion, 2.4 vs 5GHz bands."
  keywords: ["wifi router", "home network"]

- title: "Your phone battery is not dying as fast as you think"
  description: "Background refresh, screen brightness, battery health."
  keywords: ["phone charging", "smartphone battery"]
